/-!
# The base case of the `Good` framework: a coordinate ball

`Work.Cohomology.Good N c W hW` is the elementwise form of "the duality map with compact
supports `H^k_c(W) → H_{N-k}(W)`, `x ↦ x ⌢ μ_W`, is bijective" (see `Work.Cohomology.pd_good`).

This file proves the base case: for the coordinate ball

`U = e ⁻¹' Metric.ball (e z) (r/2) ∩ e.source`        (`e = chartAt _ z`, `Metric.ball (e z) r ⊆ e.target`)

we have `Good N c U`, where `c ∈ H_N(M;ℤ)` is a class whose image in `H_N(M, M∖{x})` generates for
every point `x` (`hc`, i.e. `c` is a fundamental class).

## The proof

`U` is homeomorphic to an open ball, hence contractible, with `H_m(U) = 0` for `m ≥ 1`; the compact
subsets of `U` that matter are the concentric closed balls `K_ρ`, for which

* `H_i(U, U∖K_ρ) = 0` for `i ≠ N` and `≅ ℤ` for `i = N` (chart + excision + `Duality.ball_local_homology`),
* the local fundamental class of `c` at `K_ρ` generates `H_N(U, U∖K_ρ)` (`local_generator_ball`
  transported along excision).

* the *surjectivity* clause `Good.hit`: for `k = N` it is the bijectivity of `x ↦ x ⌢ μ_{K_{r/4}}`
  from `pd_coordinate_ball_fundamental` (applied with `r/2`), for `k ≠ N` the target `H_{N-k}(U)`
  vanishes;
* the *injectivity* clause `Good.kill`: for a compact `K ⊆ U` choose a concentric closed ball
  `K' ⊇ K` (with radius in `[r/4, r/2)`); for `k ≠ N` the source `H^k(U,U∖K')` vanishes, and for
  `k = N` the map `x ↦ x ⌢ μ_{K'}` is bijective because `μ_{K'}` generates `H_N(U,U∖K') ≅ ℤ`
  (`relCapPair_top_bijective`, the universal-coefficient computation of the top-degree cap product).
-/

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
